{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793897066,"nonce":"wJNTjZFjc8TDr7DaBrpGUjE39CE=","message":"Indexed drop analysis is ready to land. It uses the existing Users operand index to enumerate only relevant instruction positions, deduplicates aliases, and preserves block insertion order and instruction order. Phi checks, terminators, classifiers, early escape/multiblock decisions and rebuilding after inserted releases are unchanged. The instruction classifier already returns None for instructions with no derived operands, so skipping those preserves its decisions.\n\n43 focused checks passed (33 drop-analysis unit tests, 4 cross-backend owned-phi tests, 6 TS ownership tests). Lua 46 conformance groups and foreign/native-snapshot checks, Python 50 groups and foreign, TS conformance wrapper and 1413 local profile cases passed. Complete pinned official TS: 5948 files, 6825 cases, PASS 1151 / FAIL 12 / UNSUPPORTED 2234 / SKIP 3428; zero regressions and identical case statuses, options, source hashes and corpus metadata to the previous validated run. Baseline unchanged. All-target clippy with LLVM/allocation-audit, formatting and diff checks passed.\n\nSynthetic pass-only timing: 2048 unrelated arithmetic instructions and 256 escaping allocations, 21 alternating runs per arm, median 4.395166 -\u003e 0.192541 ms. This fixture does not represent whole-kernel wall time. All 17 NUC optimized HIR bodies match after ID normalization, with equal inventories and optimizer progress. Instrumented drop pass medians (ms): method_call 0.95 -\u003e 0.82; op_overload 0.01 -\u003e 0.01; records 0.41 -\u003e 0.38; tokenize 0.58 -\u003e 0.50. Diagnostic runs disable OSR/snapshots symmetrically; separate normal-environment controls verify snapshot placement for both binaries. Phase sums exclude interleaved codegen lines.\n\nNUC ordinary wall time: frozen baseline 9a8a97528f812dc63070e62eaa2e28ada602f47b and candidate, LLVM off, native snapshots enabled, normal tiering, alternating pairs, CPU affinity and idle/thermal gates. Builds finish before timing; no Cargo/rustc between samples. 21 pairs x 9 workloads = 378 clean samples; all output references and throttle-delta checks pass. Initial medians (ms): method_call 28.125 -\u003e 28.560; op_overload 32.125 -\u003e 32.617; binary_trees 145.269 -\u003e 145.117; records 79.225 -\u003e 80.814; pipeline 319.462 -\u003e 317.184; tokenize 102.679 -\u003e 103.433; collatz 142.605 -\u003e 142.320; method_short 19.397 -\u003e 19.249; method_long 45.759 -\u003e 45.361. Most differences are within noise; the long method-call paired ratio is 0.99409 with exploratory 95% bootstrap interval 0.98350..0.99726. No broad wall-speedup claim.\n\nFresh control: 31 pairs each for method_call, op_overload and records = 186 further clean samples. Medians (ms): method_call 28.009 -\u003e 27.318; op_overload 31.869 -\u003e 32.516; records 81.140 -\u003e 80.892. The method-call/records slowdowns do not repeat. Operator-overload retains a slower estimate: pooled 52-pair median ratio 1.01516 with batch-stratified bootstrap interval 0.99691..1.02848. That remains inconclusive, not proof of a regression or equivalence. Keep monitoring it under parent 1be184c; no generated-HIR change or increased main-body drop time was observed.\n\nEvidence directory: /private/tmp/zyntax-drop-use-index (source/binary manifests, tests, corpus comparisons, synthetic timings, raw NUC samples, HIR and phase/paired analyses). Remote evidence: /tmp/zyntax-drop-use-index on nuc. Completed NUC archive: /private/tmp/zyntax-drop-use-index/zyntax-drop-use-index-evidence.tar.gz, SHA256 461fe3cfcc4f2f65807905f8605a5bfc3af382d7b82f5b77b5fc6309ffccaba5. Reservation released. Preexisting .gitignore edit is untouched.\n\nRemaining work: main-body drop analysis still costs 0.82 ms for method_call. The multiblock drop_points_transferring_with_uses fallback still scans instructions and reconstructs reachability/liveness per site; phis_using_any also scans all phis. These are separate opportunities with CFG/index invalidation requirements, not addressed by this slice. Parent 1be184c stays open.","files":null}]}